      "Vol. II — On the famous remissions: every 'healed' pilgrim the Gloam parades was sick with something the Warren itself causes — the weeping sores, the whispering dreams, the second pulse. The cure and the complaint share an address. The Throne's physicians treat the same cases with soap, rest, and distance from the Warren, and the recovery rate is better, and the patients keep their original eyes.\n\nA patient from the lowland villages arrived with three pupils in each eye. He claimed the walls had whispered the secrets of the stars. He was treated with caustic soap and silence until his sight returned to normal.\n\nThe ink here is faded, appearing almost grey. A cross-reference points to a lost medical treatise: [see Volume IX: On the Purging of Void-Sores], though no such book remains in the archives.\n\nThe Pale Liturgy would call these sores a blessing from the grave-kings. We call them an infection of the spirit. Soap is the only prayer a sick man needs.",
